	"effects": [
		{
			"type": "enchantment",
			"name": "Empowered Cantrips (Fire Bolt)",
			"img": "icons/magic/fire/projectile-fireball-smoke-orange-red.webp",
			"disabled": false,
			"transfer": false,
			"_id": "tj8wN1w8wdnViMY6",
			"system": {
				"changes": [
					{
						"phase": "initial",
						"priority": null,
						"_id": "7NuMyb4MktNAXAj9",
						"conditions": "{}",
						"replacement": "",
						"key": "system.description.value",
						"type": "override",
						"value": "<p><em>Muttering a short invocation and pointing at your target, you send a bolt of fire streaking forward.</em></p><p><strong>Ranged Spell Attack</strong></p><p>If this spell damages a vehicle or object that is flammable and has hit points, the object is set on fire**.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Hit:</strong> Target takes [[/damage 1d12 fire]] damage*</p></li></ul><p><strong>*At Higher Levels:</strong> This spell's damage increases by 1d12 when you reach a total character or creature level of 5th level ([[/damage 2d12 fire]]), 11th level ([[/damage 3d12 fire]]), and 17th level ([[/damage 4d12 fire]]).</p><p><em>**Some objects may be too large or flammable to be simply extinguished as an action, and will require creative solutions. Additionally, some vehicles or other objects may have a 'damage threshold'. For example, a fire bolt would have to deal at least 5 damage to damage and ignite a wooden catapult. Once ignited, the ignited object takes [[/damage 1d10 fire]] damage at the end of each of the caster's turns, which is dealt regardless of the target's damage threshold.</em></p>"
					},
					{
						"phase": "initial",
						"priority": null,
						"_id": "qPJCKTVtL6gqfohw",
						"conditions": "{}",
						"replacement": "",
